  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1132 AM CDT Tue Jun 23 2026\n\nA more zonal upper level pattern begins on Thursday, and with it \ncomes the heat. 850mb winds will turn more southwesterly, advecting \nin heat to the mid-state. Highs through Saturday will gradually \ncreep into the upper 80s and low 90s. The more zonal pattern will \nalso lend to more rain chances into the weekend, as shortwaves can \neasily pass through the area. Low to medium rain chances are \nexpected through Saturday, with QPF looking to be under an inch \ntotal across the area. At this time, we're not expecting any severe \nweather with these shortwaves, but we will let you know if that \nchanges. \n\nA high pressure system builds right over the southeastern United \nStates Sunday into Monday, intensifying the heat. Highs will stay in \nthe low to mid 90s, eventually building into the upper 90s, with \nheat indices in the triple digits. Make sure you remember to stay \ncool and take breaks in the AC or shade if you're working outside.",
